{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>El who brought him out.</b> The meaning: for El who brought him out of Egypt gave him strength like the horns of a wild ox. Let no disputant dispute on account of the mem of אל מוציאם, and think that the word לו is a sign for the name, for such is the rule of the language, like תכו לרגליך, ישא מדברותיך, עד אנה ינאצוני העם הזה, and many like these:" "<b>He will devour the nations, his adversaries.</b> The kings of Canaan:" "<b>And their bones he will crush.</b> He will break the bone, which is the עצם, and likewise the word עצמו. And thus מסעף פארה לא תפאר." "<b>And his arrows he will shatter.</b> Every arrow — מחציו he will shatter. And thus וצדיקים ככפיר יבטח, נות צעדה, and thus מברכיך ברוך — each one of those who bless you shall be blessed, and likewise אורריך."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra dismisses those who would emend the suffix and read לו as a divine name; he preserves the text as לו with mem preserved, citing analogous constructions.", 2 "The last citation appears to be a truncated or elliptic biblical paraphrase; rendered hyper-literally as the syntax is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:21.278233606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}